## Promotion

**Accept `POLAR-CONDUCTOR / UNBOUNDED-GAUGE` at the stated bounded-category scope.**

- `C_p=(g, y/D)` lies in `Z_p⟨x,y⟩^2`, reduces to `(x-x^p,y)`, and has `det J=1` as a restricted-series identity. Over `Qpbar`, `D` is reduced, with exactly `p-1` vertical components at valuation `-1/(p-1)`, outside the closed unit bidisc. This is an affine polar divisor, not projective infinity and not `A_infinity`.
- For every polynomial `φ=(X,Y)` with `det J(φ)=1` — invertibility not assumed — `gcd(D(X),Y)=1`. Automorphisms make `Pol` an isomorphic pullback invariant; Keller right maps give only non-cancellation.
- The confirmed wild theorem supplies a unique identity-branch restricted-analytic symplectic automorphism in the orientation `C_p ∘ Φ_F = F`. Reverse composition, rationality, polynomiality, a global degree drop, and deck descent are not inserted.
- Canonical conductors `κ_n(F)` tend to infinity. A uniform degree bound, or a uniform nested-support-cardinality bound, would make `Φ_F` polynomial and contradict no-cancellation. That is not a growth rate and not nonexistence of a polynomial lift.
